    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7f5e5254_42be7b46",
        "filename": "microdroid_manager/src/swap.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 90,
      "author": {
        "id": 1935515
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-12T12:37:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is safe because no data space is allocated when ZRAM is initialised. We may want to cut this to a percentage of total RAM in future? Or be configurable.",
      "parentUuid": "b4106606_960e2ad4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 90,
        "startChar": 34,
        "endLine": 90,
        "endChar": 66
      },
      "revId": "715060d5ca9b72d2821490c821ac4603a1f3d605",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "61294209_73a9cc6c",
        "filename": "microdroid_manager/src/swap.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 90,
      "author": {
        "id": 1935515
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-12T13:32:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The overhead is expected to be ~0.1% of the ZRAM disksize, if no swap is actually being used. Eg. 100MB VM -\u003e 100kB ZRAM overhead. So it\u0027s not too bad. But we can cut it a bit (eg. disksize \u003d VM RAM size / 2) if we want.",
      "parentUuid": "7f5e5254_42be7b46",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 90,
        "startChar": 34,
        "endLine": 90,
        "endChar": 66
      },
      "revId": "715060d5ca9b72d2821490c821ac4603a1f3d605",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "69868815_a512a037",
        "filename": "microdroid_manager/src/swap.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 90,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-12T13:59:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So, the current setting is tuned for maximum memory saving at the expense of performance, right? I think some VMs may want different values (or perhaps turn zram swap completely off) depending on their workload. I am not saying this initial CL should address that, but wish it could be addressed in a follow-up change (if that makes sense).",
      "parentUuid": "61294209_73a9cc6c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 90,
        "startChar": 34,
        "endLine": 90,
        "endChar": 66
      },
